Greetings to all. I've come back to the group after a (according to my
best records) 9 year hiatus. I'm amazed to remember so many familiar
names (and that it's been this long!).

The recent discussion about the time elapsed since the latest official
release prompted me to download the source and try building it, in
order to play around a little. I don't have MSVC or anything with a
fancy IDE installed, but I do have djgpp, so I thought I'd give that a
shot. I had to copy a few things around manually (and move the
makefile up a directory, and a couple other silly things), but on the
whole it went smoothly - a lot less painful than when I tried to make
the current version build with mpw (which was not officially
supported) on my Mac back in the day (I gave up on that). However, I'm
finding that the result has some annoying differences from the
official Windows binary:

1) It's *much* less responsive, even in normal dungeon conditions,
even after hacking the Makefile to apply compiler optimizations
globally (GCC = gcc -O3). I would think that Nethack ought not to
require significant CPU resources on today's machines - though
responsiveness != performance, so I wonder if something else has gone
wrong. The optimization flag didn't really have any noticeable effect,
so I'm thinking there is some setting adding an intentional delay
somewhere, or something like that.

2) The hilite_pet option, and highlighted text in general, seem not to
work. Everything that should be highlighted is just in plain text.
Foreground colours work, though. Possibly related to this, a line from
my old defaults.nh:

OPTIONS=videocolors:4-2-6-9-5-3-15-12-10-14-9-13-11,videoshades:light
light light

was causing errors (an error message for the videoshades part, and the
videocolors option appears to permute colours in an undesired way). I
took this out, but highlights still don't work.

3) Clicking the close box for the window doesn't save and quit as with
the official Windows (TTY) build, but instead pops up the usual
Windows "Windows cannot end this program" dialog.

How might I resolve these issues? Should I be emailing the devteam
directly instead of asking here?

Thanks for any assistance,
